  "question": {
    "text": "Number of integral terms in the expansion of <math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mroot><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mroot></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>1024</mn></mrow></msup></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "129",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We have,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></msub><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>5</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1024</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><msup><mfenced><mn>7</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac></msup></math><br />This is an integer, if&nbsp;<math><mn>1024</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> is an even number and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> is a multiple&nbsp;of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math></p><p>i.e. when <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> is a multiple of <math><mn>8</mn></math> since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1024</mn></math></p><p>The number of multiples of <math><mn>8</mn></math> which lies between <math><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><mn>1024</mn></math> is<br /><math><mn>1024</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>8</mn></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1024</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>129</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
